-### Formulas
-
-*   **World Position:**
-    $$
-    P_{world} = P_{min} + \frac{I_{voxel}}{N_{dim}} \times (P_{max} - P_{min})
-    $$
-    Where $I_{voxel}$ is the integer voxel coordinate, $N_{dim}$ is the grid dimension, and $P_{min}, P_{max}$ are the world-space bounds [S4, unofficial].
-
-*   **Face Culling/Orientation:**
-    Compute local camera vector:
-    $$
-    L_{cam} = C_{eye} - P_{world}
-    $$
-    For a vertex at local coordinate $v \in \{-1, 1\}^3$, the face is visible if the dot product of the face normal and view vector is positive. The source [S2, unofficial] implements this by flipping the vertex coordinate based on the sign of $L_{cam}$ components:
-    ```glsl
-    if (local_camera_pos.x > 0.0) xyz.x = 1 - xyz.x;
-    if (local_camera_pos.y > 0.0) xyz.y = 1 - xyz.y;
-    if (local_camera_pos.z > 0.0) xyz.z = 1 - xyz.z;
-    ```
-    This effectively selects the face closest to the camera [S2, unofficial].
-
-*   **Vertex Transformation:**
-    $$
-    V_{clip} = M_{VP} \times (V_{local} \times 0.05 + P_{world})
-    $$
-    Where $V_{local}$ is the unit cube vertex (scaled by 0.05 in the source [S2, unofficial]) and $M_{VP}$ is the Model-View-Projection matrix [S2, unofficial].
-
-*   **Albedo Unpacking (R5G6B5):**
-    ```glsl
-    uint u_red = (u_albedo & uint(31));
-    uint u_green = (u_albedo & uint(2016)) >> uint(5);
-    uint u_blue = (u_albedo & uint(63488)) >> uint(11);
-    vec3 albedo = vec3(float(u_red)/32.0, float(u_green)/64.0, float(u_blue)/32.0);
-    ```
-    [S2, unofficial]
-
-### Parameters
-*   **Lighting Constants:** Ambient Intensity = 0.35f, Specular Intensity = 0.5f, Shininess = 32f [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Light Position:** World-space light position at {10f, 15f, 10f} [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Zoom Clamping:** MIN_ZOOM = 0.3f, MAX_ZOOM = 3.0f [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Rotation Sensitivity:** 0.4f degrees per pixel [S1, unofficial].
-
-### Edge Cases and Pitfalls
-*   **VAO Availability:** On Android OpenGL ES 3.0, VAOs are not universally supported; explicit VBO/EBO binding may be required every frame, though overhead is negligible due to single draw call [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Zoom Artifacts:** Extreme zoom levels cause scaling artifacts; zoom factor must be clamped [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Rotation Direction:** Drag direction across screen halves affects rotation direction, handled naturally by the sign of the delta x [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Precision:** Bit-packing in SSBO requires careful bitmasks to avoid data corruption [S2, unofficial].
